{"type":"message","id":"8ce18f11","parentId":"e49da370","timestamp":"2026-03-18T16:29:53.107Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0fbce8392a27b77c0169bad2f40a1c8191b3fb8a58f6b5df97\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABputL07DsUTd4HEKd2kiRuQyO4JdCBbPwXfpLZdzfbsvAF8cWUEOdIYBggDW-xQVRSbD8LuM9WvUHzNZ2h9WDM4E0rcyA13rFgU7xUdX3ztWtdCqIvNjSgfFTxQl7ZFDkk6wepuXqlnmq2dPgH_od2qQWxZaRamP7cAoFWg-33mfmWbnk8OcLncWG_1YH6j8zn0Y0mL4u01GyXphEc_fPILInh-QIqrXWe-Xe5EkDycT76vCGuQ0eBh4iiSPhrsO9c-8Aewgm-XsMVB-Uz5ZGI_gMuigwot8ng22ZilpIldWVr5WAmkbbIqFPHwPDJeZOHpImC2nQX421gszdkSLqY9k2ERz76SBsWkva-KwbUdQNAf05P8YPrHxtNf40aomQC1_VjAznohrdX93XLtn_3-SsfLQn2Hvrcw-rURGbq9PKi8ifU74BdlpWlw870H_Ac-90KqZfMzrEFxzjnm7loLvr6nG_MyWjtIEtqlPyooJ_0DBbxn8RJi34Y7uOb8dEm3UhMIvLkq_Bp-6mrRlQMQ3csYsBw9g0ZLolPkQiVXRfOKJFYSzoHT1otVAXF3Z5K5zY5e4ETEStY41z5FUCirxxurAm56roP9k31UWl3BSIQpmrnq1f1swRpvFl6SfaTU9YXr6mKY710qRemRLUBUQXlWczY3e-kMvCo06WSRmHqWGGjl01g_iM5jnDYltF-Ej2EbItUxiuEC6l8c8rQQMgkVvDHxXiPRfz1tntnT6GyXN9f1m-bIxPhHBIv1t32scxx4wMQvTWp-6NqHt8KX1Ze3GZjDIroRmccqyv2mwMRBCLPypxY4JPVI8RqpydOSkI7AsQc3s2LkzVB-wwtyod8DrbjXRNyU4jfKbvO3jB2UKE=\",\"summary\":[]}"},{"type":"text","text":"[[reply_to_current]] I ran the pipeline. The result is **not “everything is alright”** — the pipeline’s three modules all flagged a pattern **consistent with a kidney tumor**, so this should be taken seriously and reviewed by a clinician.\n\n**Kidney Cancer Detector**\n- **Kidney cancer class:** kidney_tumor\n- **Confidence:** 99.9979%\n- **Inference time:** 3.27 s\n\n**Image Analyzer**\n- **Prediction:** kidney_tumor\n- **CAM coverage:** 0.0128\n- **CAM center ratio:** 0.825\n- **CAM left-right asymmetry:** 0.10\n- **CAM top-bottom asymmetry:** 1.00\n- **CAM explanation:** the model focused on a small, fairly central region in the kidney image, with asymmetric distribution, which it interpreted as a localized structural abnormality.\n\n**X-AI summary**\n- The pipeline summary says the scan shows a **high-likelihood kidney cancer signal**\n- It also explicitly says this is **not a definitive diagnosis**\n- **Suggested next steps from the pipeline:** further medical evaluation, clinician consultation, and possibly additional tests such as more imaging or biopsy depending on the real clinical context\n\n**What this means clinically**\n- This is a **preliminary signal, not a diagnosis**\n- But it is **concerning enough that you should arrange prompt review by a radiologist/urologist/oncologist or the clinician who ordered the scan**\n- If this scan was already done in a medical setting, the safest next step is to have the **official radiology report** reviewed rather than relying on the model alone\n\n**Urgent red flags**\nIf you also have **severe flank pain, visible blood in urine, fever, vomiting, dizziness/fainting, marked weakness, or rapidly worsening symptoms**, seek urgent medical care.\n\nAnalyzer image:\nMEDIA:http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/admin/admin/retrieve-image-file/nodes_bucket/626130f7c71f6b9e651c76be/69b862e0a6fbd73a6254e5be/b0f1c107-0576-49f4-985a-1754b3411728.jpeg\n\nIf you want, I can next do one of these:\n1. explain these results in simpler language  \n2. help you interpret the **official CT report** if you paste it  \n3. help you prepare the **next questions for your doctor**","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0fbce8392a27b77c0169bad2f4f1e08191a3d185aaed043fbe\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":23268,"output":529,"cacheRead":9344,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":33141,"cost":{"input":0.058170000000000006,"output":0.007935,"cacheRead":0.002336,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.06844100000000002}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1773851377860}}
